This port replaces the Android UI, extension execution and mpv integration
with Dart/Flutter, portable JSON catalogs and platform video playback.
It is not a release by the upstream Anikku maintainers.

flutter-tvos: https://github.com/fluttertv/flutter-tvos (BSD-3-Clause).
Generated tvOS runner files originate from that toolchain's templates.
flutter-tvos is an independent community project, not an official Google
or Apple Flutter target. Its license is included in docs/flutter-tvos.LICENSE.

The sample catalog links to Big Buck Bunny (2008), Sintel (2010), and
Tears of Steel (2012), © Blender Foundation, licensed CC BY 3.0.
https://www.blender.org/about/projects/
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
The first two samples are trailers hosted by W3C; the third is the full film
hosted by Blender. Media is streamed from those providers, not redistributed.
The assets/test/playback.mp4 color-pattern/sine clip is generated locally
with FFmpeg solely for deterministic playback testing.

Namakura Gatana (The Dull Sword), 1917, Junichi Kouchi.
Public-domain Japanese animated short, streamed from Internet Archive:
https://archive.org/details/namakura-gatana-1917
Film and restoration source information:
https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kouichi_Jun%27ichi_-_Namakura_Gatana_(1917)_-_4-minute_restored_version.webm
Sample artwork is a frame from the same film.

AnimeGG source adapter: adapted to Dart from the Yuzono anime-extensions
AnimeGG extension, Apache-2.0. Changes include portable domain models, lazy
episode resolution, bounded requests, native player and download integration.
https://github.com/yuzono/anime-extensions
